<title>USA: PNC buys AAA credit card portfolios for $116.9 million.</title>
<headline>PNC buys AAA credit card portfolios for $116.9 million.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH</dateline>
<text>
<p>PNC Bank Corp. said Monday it paid $116.9 million to buy the credit card portfolios of 50 American Automobile Association clubs from Mellon Bank Corp. with an outstanding balance of $771 million.</p>
<p>The bank said it paid a premium of 15.16 percent for the 1.3 million credit card accounts.</p>
<p>AAA provides travel, insurance, financial and auto-related services to 35 million members nationwide.</p>
</text>
